2.  **Fear of Consequences**: They might say, &quot;If you don't comply, this will happen&quot; or &quot;If you don't do what I say, you'll regret it.&quot;

3.  **Comparison to Others**: They might compare their relationship to others, saying &quot;I'm doing so much more for this relationship than you are,&quot; or &quot;You're lucky to have me supporting us.&quot;

4.  **Claiming Entitlement**: They might say &quot;I deserve better&quot; or &quot;You owe me.&quot;

5.  **Blaming the Victim**: They might say &quot;If you weren't so irresponsible, we wouldn't have to have this conversation&quot; or &quot;You're the one who got us into this mess.&quot;

6.  **Gaslighting**: They might say &quot;You're being paranoid&quot; or &quot;You're overreacting,&quot; making the other person doubt their own perceptions or sanity.

7.  **Minimizing**: They might say &quot;It's not that big of a deal&quot; or &quot;You're being too dramatic,&quot; downplaying the significance of the issue.

8.  **Anger or Aggression**: They might say &quot;You're making me angry&quot; or &quot;You're pushing me to my limits&quot; in an attempt to justify their behavior.

9.  **Deflecting Responsibility**: They might say &quot;You're always doing this&quot; or &quot;This is all your fault,&quot; deflecting responsibility for their actions.

10. **Shaming**: They might say &quot;You're so selfish&quot; or &quot;You're not a good partner,&quot; making the other person feel guilty or ashamed.

